      "text": "•1-2 Slides ( with Tables/ chart/ graphs )\n\nModel Performance Evaluation: We used a Bidirectional LSTM model because, unlike a standard LSTM that only looks at past data, BiLSTM processes the sequence both forward and backward.\n\nThis means it not only understands how past user interactions influence future sales, but also how future patterns or trends can provide context for earlier data points.\n\nResults: \nTo evaluate our model’s performance, we used key statistical measures that show how well the predictions align with real sales data:\n\nStrong positive correlation (r = 0.82) between predicted and actual sales.\t\nR2 Score = 0.9620 (captures fluctuations/variance in sales is captured by the model)\nRMSE(Root Mean Squared Error) = 6.5%  (very low prediction error)\nAverage Sales= 75847.19\n\nOverall, a strong correlation (r=0.82), high R² (0.962), and low RMSE (6.5%) together confirm that our BiLSTM model accurately captures real sales behavior, with minimal deviation from actual performance.\n",
